The motivation underlying the study of fluctuations is to identify critical fluctuations. However, hadronic processes like resonance decay can also influence the particle-ratio fluctuations. To better understand the origin of the observed signal for fluctuations, separate sign fluctuations are also measured for STAR data. Because the \(K^{-}\) and \(\bar{p}\) yields go to zero at low energies, we will present only \(K^{+}\) and \(p\) related fluctuations.

