The balance functions in terms of \(q_{\rm side}\) do not look like those measured using \(q_{\rm long}\) or \(q_{\rm out}\) because the lower momentum cut-off of STAR strongly affects \(B(q_{\rm side})\) for \(q_{\rm side}<0.38\) GeV/\(c\), which underscores the importance of performing comparisons with models that have been put through detailed efficiency and acceptance filters.

