The dramatically tight correlations in \(\Delta\phi\) in central collisions of Au+Au shown in Fig. 6.13 are qualitatively consistent with the radial flow of a perfect liquid. In a liquid with very short mean free path, the balancing particles would remain in close proximity throughout the reaction. A large mean free path, which would necessitate a large viscosity, would damp the correlations in \(\Delta\phi\)[64]. This trend is also consistent with a picture where charges are not created until after the flow has been established.

