A similar trend is also observed for other centralities. Figure 6.29 shows the same analysis for nine centralities from most central (0-5%) to most peripheral (70%-80%) collisions. All three cases show peak structures in central collisions, which is due to strong collective flow. The asymmetry of the \(\phi=45^{\circ}\) balance function is most significant at mid-central collisions, where the elliptic flow is strongest.

To quantify the effect of collective flow on the balance function, we present the weighted average cosine, \(c_{b}(\phi)\), and weighted average sine, \(s_{b}(\phi)\), extracted from the balance functions.

